p2p notes

goal: server will now relay blocks instead of storing actual data

add direct connection stuff later, focus now on relaying

clients drain journals based on "transfers complete"
when it comes to incoming changes we keep that behavior

sending out blocks from our journal, we delete on fetch
we cannot do that because not everyone gets the block
need a way to signal that a client can drop journal blocks

add to the lockstate a list of who we are waiting on for a done message


all that remains is making the relay stream

clients receive data through manifests and deltas
these objects will have an origin attached to them
    if many clients are requesting directly from the origin will that overwhelm the origin?
    maybe the server can cache blocks if they are requested often?
    
right now: 
the server journals blocks until the transfer is complete
then it stores the blocks into the main block table
    as a relay it will instead not journal anything bc it will not store anything, 
    applying the manifest to the block table directly
